---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { href } from '../../lib/href';
import Widget from '../../components/DiagramDecomposition.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Block Diagram to Equations — ECE/ME 732">
  <p class="crumb"><a href={href("/interactives/")}>← Interactives</a></p>
  <h1>Block Diagram to Equations</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    A state block diagram is a set of equations drawn as a picture. Cut it into
    regions, write the one equation each region stands for, then eliminate the
    signals in between. Five practice systems, from one state to nonlinear.
  </p>
  <p class="hint">
    Reading rules used throughout: a summing junction is an equals sign whose
    output is the signed sum of its inputs; a block multiplies its input by what
    is written inside it; <i>1/s</i> integrates, and every integrator output is a
    state; a nonlinear block applies its function to its inputs rather than
    multiplying. Hover a card to find its region, or click a region to jump to its card.
  </p>
  <Widget />
</BaseLayout>
